    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the welcome-notification side effect for successful owner creation.\n\n**What I added:**\n- `EnqueueWelcomeNotification.java` \u2014 a new OfficeFloor function that reads the saved `Owner` via `@Val` and emits a line to the `NOTIFY` logger containing both the owner id and the `memberId`:\n  ```\n  NOTIFY - Welcome notification enqueued: id=11 memberId=NSW2716E6609E1\n  ```\n- Wired it into `owners.POST.yml` as the `enqueueWelcome` step, placed after the audit-event step and before `respond`. It runs after `SaveOwner` (so the generated id and assigned member id are available) and carries `govern: [ transaction ]` consistent with the surrounding create steps.\n\nThe function mirrors the existing `LogOwnerCreatedEvent`/`LogOwnerAudit` pattern (a named SLF4J logger, single public `service` method, `@Val Owner`), so it only fires on the successful-create path.\n\n`./mvnw test` is green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest.coreEnqueuesWelcome` (the only test class) passes, asserting the `NOTIFY` log line contains the fetched owner's id and memberId.",
